<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="079" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Deploy WP3 to dev</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — wave W3-5</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deployment and smoke verification of already-reviewed tasks; no new code.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Prescriptive deploy procedure using existing scripts and skills.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Writes to the shared dev environment (BFF app service, Dataverse rows and web resources).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>070, 071, 072, 073, 074, 075, 076, 077, 078, 053, 080, 081, 082, 083, 084, 085, 086, 087</deps>
    <tags>deploy, bff, code-page</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Deploy WP3 to dev — the BFF with the rules system, the BILLING-RULE-DRAFT@v1 Action and Binding, the rule-type option values and the Rule Review code page — then smoke-test every new route and publish a real outside-counsel-guideline rule set in dev whose rules all cite their clauses.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the bff-deploy, code-page-deploy and dataverse-deploy procedures and dev smoke verification.</role>

  <goal>Dev runs WP3: new routes answer 401 unauthenticated and the expected status authenticated; one real OCG rule set is drafted, reviewed and published with clause citations; a sample rate card is imported and published; evidence recorded in task notes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec WP3 (FR-24 – FR-30), success criterion 3 (an admin uploads an OCG and publishes a rule set where every rule cites its clause), project CLAUDE.md section 5 (dev only; deploys only inside named deploy tasks; scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1 for the BFF; scripts/Import-SolutionScoped.ps1 is the only solution import path). Evaluation-set OCGs come from task 002 (projects/ebilling-r1/notes/evaluation-set/manifest.md). WP2 (053) is deployed first. Web resources deploy with scripts/Deploy-WebResourceInline.ps1 (parameters DataverseUrl, WebResourceName, FilePath). Action mirrors deploy with scripts/Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1; Bindings with scripts/dataverse/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1. Rule-type options: 070's scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleTypeOptions.ps1.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="read">scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/Deploy-WebResourceInline.ps1</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/dataverse/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleTypeOptions.ps1</file>
      <file role="read">src/solutions/RuleReview/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="070-078" status="pending">All WP3 tasks complete and merged to the branch</dependency>
      <dependency task="053" status="pending">WP2 deployed to dev</dependency>
      <dependency task="080-087" status="pending">Rule-set scope (D-136 / D-137 / D-141; notes/rule-set-scope-design.md section 10): 080 schema on dev (S1-S4, S6-S8), 081-087 code merged (081 and 086 ran their secure-family probes and creator-person -Apply on dev with the owner's OK; 087 approved by uac-r2). Folded into this deploy because 079 had not run.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md section 5">Dev only. No production or customer environment. No secrets in the repo or notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md">Deploy the BFF only with scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1 and its hash verification; never trust a success message alone.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No destructive Dataverse change. Option values and rows are additive; -WhatIf first where the script supports it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This serial deploy task may edit SpaarkeMaster solution source (project CLAUDE.md §3): additive sitemap / navigation entries for the Rule Review page and any WP3 columns or tables added after 029 (e.g. 070's rule-type option values, 019 / 076 additions), using 029's export-to-temp procedure, verified with Import-SolutionScoped.ps1 -PlanOnly. Anything non-additive follows the escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Never delete the owner-created containers or evaluation-set documents.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-114 (owner)">The Rule Review page (web resource sprk_rulereviewpage, from 077) gets two entry points: a "Rule Review" subarea in the Spaarke Administration app's sitemap, and a command on the sprk_ruleset main form that opens the page for that rule set (pass the rule set id). Both go in solution-scoped through scripts/Import-SolutionScoped.ps1. Verify both open the page on dev.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-113 (owner)">Before the BFF that reads it is deployed, run the 077 follow-up's idempotent schema script for the rejection-reason column (WhatIf first). 053 must already have synced it into SpaarkeMaster.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172, tasks 080-085 (rule-set scope)">SpaarkeMaster sync (029 export-to-temp, additive only) of 080's schema: sprk_ruleset sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_workassignment lookups (RemoveLink), the Record and FirmRecord sprk_scope options, sprk_allbusinessunits, the sprk_ruleset_businessunit N:N (subgrid on the rule set main form), and sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope (on the rate card main form and its views). Two admin system views: "Rule sets whose record was deleted" (sprk_ruleset: scope Record or FirmRecord, all three core lookups empty) and "Rate cards whose record was deleted" (sprk_ratecard: scope CoreRecord, all three core lookups empty). Immediately before deploying the BFF, re-run the S6 backfill section of scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1 (WhatIf first; idempotent, fills only empty scopes) so no card the old import created in between applies to nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-141, uac-r2 review items 3-6 (design note sections 2 S5/S7/S8/S9, 5.4)">The S7 columns (sprk_ruleset sprk_scope, sprk_firm and the three core lookups) are field-secured, everyone Read and BFF write: on the rule set main form they show read-only, and SpaarkeMaster carries their field-security profile entries (additive). The S8 column sprk_securedfrombusinessunit (sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_workassignment) is synced into SpaarkeMaster with its field security but placed on NO form and in NO view. Immediately before Deploy-BffApi.ps1, the secure family must be live: scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -Verify passes for the rule set, policy, policy version, rate card and rate rows (if not: -WhatIf, then -Apply with the owner's OK, then -Verify), and scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 -Verify passes for the tables 081 and 086 added. A BFF whose census and lineage name those tables must not run against an environment whose roles and columns lack them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="076 re-check K2">Before relying on 076's conditional publish, make one probe on dev, with the owner's OK for the live write. It confirms that IfRowVersionMatches inside ExecuteTransactionRequest is honoured per inner request and that the mismatch fault carries 0x80060882.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/code-page-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/CLAUDE.md (section 5)</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Preconditions: every dependency shows ✅ in TASK-INDEX.md; git merge-base --is-ancestor f292ad119 HEAD succeeds; dotnet build and dotnet test green on the branch; record the commit SHA.</step>
    <step order="2">Rule-type options: run Deploy-EbillingRuleTypeOptions.ps1 with -WhatIf, then for real if anything is missing; verify the 11 billing values by metadata read.</step>
    <step order="3">Action and Binding: run Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 for billing-rule-draft and Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1; verify both rows with a Dataverse read query (actioncode, consumer type, environment).</step>
    <step order="4">BFF: run scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1 against spaarke-bff-dev; confirm hash verification passed and /healthz is healthy; confirm the eBilling flag is on in dev.</step>
    <step order="3a">Rule-set scope schema: confirm 080's items on dev by metadata read (S7 field security on the five sprk_ruleset columns; S8 field-secured with no reader profile); sync them, the S7/S8 field-security profile entries and the two "record deleted" views into SpaarkeMaster (export-to-temp, Import-SolutionScoped.ps1 -PlanOnly first; S7 read-only on the rule set form, S8 on no form and in no view); then re-run the S6 backfill section (WhatIf, then for real) and record the cards it filled, if any.</step>
    <step order="3b">Secure family (before step 4): run Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -Verify and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 -Verify; if either fails, -WhatIf (or the dry run) then -Apply with the owner's OK, then -Verify again. Record the output.</step>
    <step order="5">Code page: in src/solutions/RuleReview run npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund and npm run build; deploy the single HTML file with Deploy-WebResourceInline.ps1 (web resource name from 077's notes); publish customizations.</step>
    <step order="6">Route smoke: for every route added by 075, 076 and 078 call once unauthenticated (expect 401) and once as a billing admin (expect 200 or 202); call one write route as a non-admin (expect 403). Record status codes.</step>
    <step order="6a">Rule-set scope smoke: create a matter-scoped Draft rule set from the Rule Review page (record picker), publish it, and submit or re-evaluate one invoice on that matter and one on a project filed directly under it: its rule judges both (findings cite its policy). Confirm a change of scope on the Published set returns 409 ruleset.scope_locked. Confirm a firm-wide rate card still resolves for an invoice of its firm.</step>
    <step order="7">End-to-end: create a rule set from a real OCG in the evaluation set (Guideline, client default); trigger drafting; when the job completes open the Rule Review page, accept at least three proposals and edit one, publish with an effective date. Verify each published version has clause quote and location, the rule set flag is on, and editing a published rule creates a new version.</step>
    <step order="8">Rate card: download the template, import a sample card (one deliberately bad row first: expect per-row error and nothing written), import the corrected workbook, publish; verify the workbook is in the Procedure Library container.</step>
    <step order="9">Run the 077 ui-tests against dev (including dark mode) and record the results.</step>
    <step order="10">Record evidence (commit SHA, script outputs summarised, status codes, record ids, screenshots paths) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/079-wp3-deploy.md.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="12">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any deploy script fails or hash verification fails, STOP; do not retry blindly or deploy by another route. Report the output.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any smoke route returns 500, or a non-admin call succeeds, STOP and report — do not continue to the end-to-end step.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a needed SpaarkeMaster change is not additive (it would alter or remove an existing component, or touch another project's components), STOP and ask the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a published rule lacks a clause citation, STOP: success criterion 3 is not met; report which proposal and rule set.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">deploy scripts</tool>
    <tool name="npm">build</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">read_query verification</tool>
    <tool name="ui-test">browser checks</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/079-wp3-deploy.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Deploy-BffApi.ps1 completed with hash verification passed; /healthz healthy after deploy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The 11 billing rule-type option values, the BILLING-RULE-DRAFT@v1 Action and its Binding exist in dev (read-query evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every new WP3 route returns 401 unauthenticated and 200 or 202 for an admin; a non-admin write returns 403 (recorded per route).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">One real OCG rule set is published in dev with every published rule carrying a clause quote and location; editing a published rule created a new version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A rate card import with a bad row returned per-row errors and wrote nothing; the corrected import and publish succeeded with the workbook stored in the Procedure Library container.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">077 ui-tests pass in dev, including dark mode.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">080's schema and the two "record deleted" views are in SpaarkeMaster (PlanOnly evidence); the S6 backfill re-run left no card with an empty scope except those with two or more core lookups.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Before the BFF deploy, Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -Verify and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 -Verify both passed (output recorded); the S7 controls are read-only on the rule set form and sprk_securedfrombusinessunit is on no form and in no view (PlanOnly and metadata evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 6a also shows: a Make Secure on a dev test matter wrote its prior business unit into sprk_securedfrombusinessunit (087), and an id-keyed rule-set route on a set the caller cannot read answers 404 (081).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The step 6a smoke passed: the matter-scoped set judged the matter's and its direct project's invoices; the Published set's scope change returned 409; a firm-wide rate card resolved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Evidence recorded in notes/079-wp3-deploy.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Shared dev environment: coordinate timing with other projects deploying spaarke-bff-dev. Publish-size was measured per task; record the deployed package size here for the cumulative NFR-12 view.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
